      {
        "name": "binary_choice",
        "description": "Show two large overlay SENTENCE BUTTONs IMMEDIATELY. Use when SOMEONE ELSE offers the user a choice between two options — either a binary choice (\"Do you want the apple or the banana?\", or holds up two objects) OR a yes/no question. For yes/no, use the canonical `yes` / `no` SYMBOLs (e.g. option1=\"Yes|yes||Yes\", option2=\"No|no||No\") — they render with the animated yes/no icons and default green/red coloring. A \"Neither\" button is added automatically. Do NOT use for open-ended questions — use the USER RESPONSE BOARD for those.",
        "behavior": "NON_BLOCKING",
        "parametersJsonSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "option1": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "speech|sentence|fallback|label — same ${T.button} format as rebuild_board. All ${T.button} rules apply (multi-glyph SENTENCEs, MODIFIER SYMBOLs, OPERATORs, fallback when `sentence` uses `generate:`). speech is the first-person SENTENCE the user voices on press. label is the short on-button text. For yes/no questions, use the `yes` / `no` canonical SYMBOLs — they animate on hover and auto-color the ${T.button} green / red without you setting an explicit color. Examples: \"כן|yes||כן\", \"לא תודה|no.please||לא תודה\", \"אני רוצה את התפוח|i_me+want+🍎||תפוח\", \"אני רוצה לשחק בחוץ|i_me+want+play+🌳||בחוץ\"."
            },
            "option2": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "speech|sentence|fallback|label — same ${T.button} format as rebuild_board. All ${T.button} rules apply (multi-glyph SENTENCEs, MODIFIER SYMBOLs, OPERATORs, fallback when `sentence` uses `generate:`). speech is the first-person SENTENCE the user voices on press. label is the short on-button text. For yes/no questions, use the `yes` / `no` canonical SYMBOLs — they animate on hover and auto-color the ${T.button} green / red without you setting an explicit color. Examples: \"כן|yes||כן\", \"לא תודה|no.please||לא תודה\", \"אני רוצה את התפוח|i_me+want+🍎||תפוח\", \"אני רוצה לשחק בחוץ|i_me+want+play+🌳||בחוץ\"."
            }
